      "content": "It's understandable that you're trying to find a solution within a tight timeframe, but taking them on different schedules doesn't significantly decrease the risks associated with combining high doses of Ritalin and caffeine. The timing might slightly reduce some immediate side effects, but the individual risks still persist. It's not just about the two substances interacting at the same time; their combined effects on your system could disrupt your homeostasis, leading to unpredictable results and potentially severe consequences. What is more important is long-term health, so I would strongly advise seeking medical advice even with your upcoming exams. There might be other ways to support your study efforts that are both safe and effective. If you're feeling anxious about the exams, speaking with your school counselor or a study group could also provide valuable support. Your health is the priority here.",
